budgie-desktop (10.7-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Upload to unstable
  * Patches added
    - appindexer-Take-into-account-default-handlers-for-re.patch
      Adjust the relevancy score of applications relative to a search term
      based on if that application is the default handler for the MIME types
      it supports. This should make it more likely that applications set as
      default for a content type is shown above other applications.
    - feat-Automatically-update-Calendar-widget-when-showi.patch
      eliminates an unnecessary 30 second timer that existed for the purposes
      of highlighting the current day.
    - Ensure-screenshot-popover-labels-match-their-corresp.patch
      Display the correct keyboard label for the keyboard shortcut
    - Plugin-chooser-escape-description-markup-symbols-293.patch
      When a plugin has an "&" in their "description=" line in the .plugin
      file, the description fails to properly show. (set_markup error).
    - Test-if-the-window-of-type-desktop-before-taking-a-w.patch
      Where invoking the screenshot and taking a window screenshot of an
      empty desktop, the empty desktop displaying icons is actually a
      hidden window.  In this case we should take a full screenshot.
    - appindexer-Check-if-an-application-name-contains-a-s.patch
      make it easier to find applications by only typing a part of the
      application's name.
  * Packaging Changes:
    - update missing libbudgie-appindexer0 symbols

 -- David Mohammed <fossfreedom@ubuntu.com>  Thu, 09 Feb 2023 22:05:01 +0000

